# Build output — regenerated by `npm run build`, never edited by hand.
lib/

# Dependencies (the package declares zero runtime dependencies, but npm may
# still create this directory).
node_modules/

# Local scratch: probe scripts and measurement output. The plugin's claims are
# checkable from the source comments and the test suite; anything under
# `.scratch/` is a one-off measurement, not an input to the build.
.scratch/

# Trial-run reports: an agent driving this plugin against one idea writes a long
# Markdown report beside the code. That is an output of USING the plugin, not an
# input to it — the plugin itself never writes inside the workspace (its only
# write is the cache file under `$DSH_HOME/cache/dsh-find-ideas`, see
# `src/cache.ts`). Kept out of the repository so a trial run cannot end up in a
# commit, in the published package, or on GitHub.
*报告.md

# The A/B experiment reports used to be carved out of the rule above with `!`
# exceptions, because `eval/harness/ab-wall-clock.mjs` READS
# `v0.4.0-AB实验报告.md` to verify the retracted wall-clock claim still appears
# as a retraction, and a file absent from a fresh clone silently degraded that
# check to SKIP — a check that cannot run is how the retracted column survived a
# 28-item green gate the first time.
#
# They are no longer tracked: `05a46cd chore: 从仓库移除两份本地实验报告` took
# them out of the repository on the maintainer's decision that they are local
# records only. The exceptions therefore went with them, and the SKIP risk is
# accepted knowingly rather than reintroduced by accident: locally the reports
# are still on disk so the gate still runs, while a fresh clone reports
# `SKIP  v0.4.0-AB实验报告.md -- file absent from this checkout` instead of
# passing quietly. Restoring the two `!` lines restores the guarantee.
#
# The machine-readable half of the same baseline is still tracked under
# `eval/runs/ab-v04*-baseline/`, and `eval/harness/ab-v041.mjs` recomputes the
# v0.4.1 numbers from those files without needing either report.

# Local artefacts that are not inputs to the build and must not reach a commit
# or the published package:
#  - `lib-conc1/` is a second build output directory from a concurrency probe;
#  - `resume-output/` holds personal documents unrelated to this project;
#  - a `*技术方案.md` beside the code is a report written by USING the plugin
#    (the same category as `*报告.md` above, just a different filename);
#  - `eval/fixtures/inspect-live-shape.json` is a 600 KB raw dump captured while
#    probing the card's live shape. Nothing reads it; the fixtures the harness
#    actually consumes are `inspect-golden-raw.json` and
#    `inspect-golden-baseline.json`, both tracked.
lib-conc1/
resume-output/
*技术方案.md
eval/fixtures/inspect-live-shape.json

# Archify run receipts under `docs/`: these record the machine that ran the
# render — absolute paths under the user's home directory and the local node
# binary — which is not information the repository should carry. The diagram
# itself is tracked (`docs/dsh-find-ideas.html`, the PNG, and the candidate it
# was built from); re-running `archify finalize` regenerates these receipts on
# any machine, so nothing is lost by leaving them out.
docs/*.finalize.json
docs/*.finalize-summary.json
docs/*.browser-check.json
docs/*.delivery.json

# Archify's own run directory — the working area that produced the three files
# above. It holds the frozen candidate, a copy of the rendered HTML, the
# screenshots, and the same receipts already excluded under `docs/`, so it
# carries the same local paths. Everything worth keeping is copied into `docs/`
# and `archify render` recreates the rest, so this is regenerable output rather
# than an input.
#
# Ignoring it also matters for the test suite: `test/source-integrity.test.mjs`
# walks the tree for U+FFFD, and these receipts legitimately contain the
# replacement characters left by a GBK console reading UTF-8 paths. Untracked
# but visible, that directory failed the local suite while a fresh clone — which
# never has it — stayed green. A check that depends on whether someone happened
# to run the renderer is not a check.
.archify/

# Local editor / OS state.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The golden harness writes the baseline it is about to overwrite here
# (`--write --force` keeps the old file beside the new one). It is a one-off
# backup of a file that is itself tracked, so committing it would add a second
# copy of the same 90KB on every intentional re-record.
eval/fixtures/inspect-golden-baseline.prev.json

# Tarballs produced by `npm pack` while checking what would be published.
*.tgz
